concept:{title:"Newton's Laws Applied to Sport",definition:"Biomechanics applies classical mechanics to human movement analysis.",points:["1st Law (Inertia): a body at rest/motion stays that way unless acted on by force","2nd Law (F=ma): force equals mass times acceleration — explains why heavier shot put needs more force","3rd Law (Action-Reaction): explains starting blocks, swimming push-offs, jumping"],memoryTrick:"'3rd Law = every push has a payback (equal & opposite)'.",sportsRelevance:"Explains technique optimization in sprint starts, swimming turns, and jumping takeoffs."},
