subject:"Teaching Methods",
topic:"Command Style",
difficulty:"Moderate",
type:"MCQ",
year:2023,
question:"In Mosston's Spectrum of Teaching Styles, the 'Command Style', where the teacher makes all decisions and students simply respond, is best suited for:",
options:["Encouraging maximum student creativity","Teaching precise, safety-critical skills requiring uniform execution (e.g., gymnastics safety drills)","Independent research projects","Peer teaching only"],
correctIndex:1,
explanation:"The Command Style places all decision-making with the teacher, making it ideal for teaching precise, safety-critical or highly standardized skills where uniform, immediate execution matters most.",
concept:{title:"Mosston's Spectrum of Teaching Styles",definition:"A foundational framework in PE pedagogy classifying teaching styles by who makes the decisions — teacher or learner.",points:["Command Style: teacher decides everything, students replicate exactly","Best for safety-critical, precision-dependent skills","Contrasted with more student-centered styles like Guided Discovery"],memoryTrick:"'Command = the teacher COMMANDS, students comply.'",sportsRelevance:"Used when teaching correct spotting technique in gymnastics or safe weight-lifting form, where errors are dangerous."},
